---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import about_us_banner from "../assets/blog/about/about_us_banner.png";
import CharlieAsBlob from "../assets/blog/about/charlie_as_blob.png";
import julia_as_blob from "../assets/blog/about/julia_as_blob.png";
import Layout from "../layouts/blog-post.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="About Us"
	description="Learn about the people behind Periodt!"
	date={new Date("August 08 2021")}
	category="Info"
	image={about_us_banner}
>
	<p>Hi, we're Periodt!</p>
	<p>
		We're building a truly private period and symptom tracker. But to
		trust us, it's only natural to want to know a bit about who we are.
	</p>
	<p><strong>Julia Wisniewska</strong></p>

	<Image
		class="block mx-auto"
		width="300"
		height="300"
		src={julia_as_blob}
		alt=""
	/>
	<p>
		My rambling about how awful the privacy features and period predictions 
		in current period tracker apps are is part of what led us to develop 
		Periodt. 
		
		I’m currently studying Psychological and Behavioural Sciences at the 
		University of Cambridge, and hoping to move forward into a career in 
		Neuroscience. It hasn't been easy, especially when juggling my workload
		with my health. Regardless, I've been trying to put work into Periodt 
		wherever and whenever I can.
	</p>
	<p>
		Hearing the negative experiences that my friends had when speaking to
		healthcare professionals about period related issues made me
		apprehensive to seek help. They found it difficult to get their doctors
		to listen to their symptoms, and were often brushed off being told that
		their pain was normal, when further investigations showed that was
		certainly not the case. Through my own journey navigating the UK's NHS
		pathways for suspected endometriosis, it became clear to me that we need
		more support readily available for people who menstruate. As my friends
		did, I found that trying to advocate for yourself in medical
		environments is very difficult, especially in the midst of having health
		problems.
	</p>
	<p>
		Due to these issues, I wanted to make sure that Periodt included symptom
		tracking that let you know if any patterns were concerning, and advice
		for speaking to healthcare professionals. 
		
		I hope that Periodt helps make challenging healthcare situations a 
		little bit easier to help anyone advocating for themselves during 
		difficultdoctors appointments.
	</p>
	<p>
		My key responsibilities at Periodt include reading and organising
		research, writing most of the blogs and handling the social media
		accounts.
	</p>
	<p><strong>Charlie Wood</strong></p>

	<Image
		class="block mx-auto"
		width="300"
		height="300"
		src={CharlieAsBlob}
		alt=""
	/>
	<p>
		Helping my partner through her menstrual health problems and seeing her
		struggle with getting <del>adequate</del> any medical support is really where
		my interest in developing Periodt comes from. I hope that Periodt provides
		a safe environment for people of all ages to learn, track their symptoms and
		feel secure in the safety of their personal information.
	</p>
	<p>
		After learning about the privacy issues in
		existing period trackers and the horrific consequences that many people
		have faced, I've become increasingly interested in building a period tracker
		that is truly private in a way that cannot change.
	</p>
	<p>
		At Periodt, I handle the technical side. I've created the actual app
		itself, and will be making blogs to teach you how it all works. At times 
		I also get bullied by Julia into giving the social media marketing a try.
	</p>
	<p>
		I really hope that through Periodt, we can not only help people who
		menstruate, but increase awareness of the importance of data privacy
		especially with health data.
	</p>
</Layout>
